    <h2 id="rp-head">Which rules apply</h2>
    <p>Refunds at {{ site.name }} follow the guidelines of the {{ site.affiliation.university }} for BBA, BCA, B.Com and B.Sc Agriculture, and the applicable NCTE and Government of Uttar Pradesh rules for B.Ed, M.Ed and D.El.Ed, including the rules of the state counselling process through which the seat was allotted. Where a university or government order differs from this page, that order applies.</p>
    <p class="callout"><span class="ph">[Insert the college's approved refund schedule here: the percentage refunded against each cut-off date, measured from the last date of admission or from the date of withdrawal, as notified by the university and the state.]</span></p>

    <h2>How to withdraw an admission</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Submit a written withdrawal application to the college office, signed by the student and a parent or guardian.</li>
      <li>Attach the fee receipt and, for counselling-route programmes, the allotment letter.</li>
      <li>Collect the acknowledgement and note its date — the refund is calculated from it.</li>
      <li>Return the original documents issued to you, and clear any library or hostel dues.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What is refunded</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Tuition fee:</strong> refunded as per the schedule above.</li>
      <li><strong>Security deposit, where paid:</strong> refunded in full, less any dues. <span class="ph">[confirm]</span></li>
      <li><strong>Registration, admission processing and examination fees paid to the university:</strong> normally not refundable. <span class="ph">[confirm]</span></li>
      <li><strong>Hostel and transport charges:</strong> <span class="ph">[state the rule for part-period use]</span></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How long it takes</h2>
    <p>Approved refunds are paid by bank transfer to the account from which the fee was paid, within <span class="ph">[number]</span> working days of the withdrawal being accepted. <span class="ph">[Name the documents required for the transfer, such as a cancelled cheque or bank passbook copy.]</span></p>

    <h2>Cancellation by the college</h2>
    <p>If an admission is cancelled because a programme does not run, or because the college finds the applicant ineligible after verification, the fee paid for that session is refunded in full.</p>

